    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Mix all the filling ingredients in a bowl with your hands until well combined and slightly sticky.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Fry or microwave a teaspoon of the filling, taste it and adjust the salt and pepper before wrapping.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Separate the wrappers and keep them under a damp towel so they do not dry out.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Lay a wrapper half on the counter with the cut side facing you. Spread a heaping tablespoon of filling in a thin log along the cut edge, leaving 2 cm at each end.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Roll it up tightly, folding in the ends partway through, and seal the last edge with a dab of water. Repeat with the rest.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Heat the oil in a deep pan to 170°C (340°F). Fry the rolls in batches, turning, until deep golden and cooked through.",
        "minutes": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Drain on a rack or paper towels. Cut in half on the diagonal if you like and serve hot with sweet chili sauce.",
        "minutes": null
      }
    ],
    "tips": "Freeze uncooked rolls in a single layer on a tray, then bag them. Fry straight from frozen, adding a minute or two."
